-- An illustrative rule, not a statute: a payment of ten is split into a number
-- of equal instalments, and an instalment is large when it exceeds two, unless
-- there are more than a hundred of them.
--
-- The first condition guards the second, because dividing by zero instalments
-- has no answer: `10 / instalments` raises when `instalments` is zero.
-- That input is decided by the first condition alone, so it still has to be
-- tested, and a cover point for each condition would lose it.
@export default Whether each instalment is large
GIVEN instalments IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `instalment is large` IF
      NOT (instalments EQUALS 0)
  AND 10 / instalments GREATER THAN 2
  UNLESS instalments GREATER THAN 100
